<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cheka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–1922</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as All-Russian Extraordinary Commission</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cheka, the All-Russian Extraordinary Commission, was the first Soviet secret police, founded in December 1917 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-dzerzhinsky">Felix Dzerzhinsky</a> to fight counter-revolution and sabotage. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a> it carried out the Red Terror, with mass arrests, hostage-taking and executions without trial. In 1922 it was replaced by the GPU, a forerunner of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a> and the KGB.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cheka.jpg" alt="Cheka" width="176" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GPU_5th_anniversary_emblem.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
